From: SableOS <noreply@sableos.invalid>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 16:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1068/1068] SableOS: FM lock screen player buttons drive the radio

The FM media session only answered hardware media keys. A controller that presses the
transport buttons directly (the Sable lock screen player and other media controllers) got
no response, so previous, next and play or pause on the lock screen did nothing for FM.
The session now handles play, pause, stop, skip to next and skip to previous: the skips seek
to the next or previous station and pause and stop turn the radio off.
---
 src/com/android/fmradio/FmService.java | 32 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 32 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/com/android/fmradio/FmService.java b/src/com/android/fmradio/FmService.java
--- a/src/com/android/fmradio/FmService.java
+++ b/src/com/android/fmradio/FmService.java
@@ -1370,7 +1370,39 @@ public class FmService extends Service implements FmRecorder.OnRecorderStateChanged {
         mMediaSession.setCallback(new MediaSession.Callback() {
             @Override
             public boolean onMediaButtonEvent(Intent mediaButtonIntent) {
                 return listener.handleIntent(mediaButtonIntent);
             }
+            // SableOS: the lock screen player and other media controllers drive the radio through
+            // these callbacks, so previous, next and play or pause on the lock screen work for FM.
+            @Override
+            public void onPlay() {
+                if (mPowerStatus != POWER_UP) {
+                    powerUpAsync(FmUtils.computeFrequency(getFrequency()));
+                }
+            }
+
+            @Override
+            public void onPause() {
+                if (mPowerStatus != POWER_DOWN) {
+                    powerDownAsync();
+                }
+            }
+
+            @Override
+            public void onStop() {
+                if (mPowerStatus != POWER_DOWN) {
+                    powerDownAsync();
+                }
+            }
+
+            @Override
+            public void onSkipToNext() {
+                seekStationAsync(FmUtils.computeFrequency(mCurrentStation), true);
+            }
+
+            @Override
+            public void onSkipToPrevious() {
+                seekStationAsync(FmUtils.computeFrequency(mCurrentStation), false);
+            }
         });
         mMediaSession.setPlaybackState(new PlaybackState.Builder().setActions(
